{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>My heart wanders. Horror.</b> From ויכרות אסא את מפלצתה (1 Kings 15:13); like כדמות תפארת, for the Persians would exult — therefore I am terrified; or trembling, as in יתפלצון (Job 9:6)." "<b>The night of my desire.</b> The night in which he drank from the vessels, and terror — as Daniel called the writing (Daniel 5:3)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:27.400969302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}